### DEV / OPS

**[HB-09] CI/CD health**
```
Spawn subagent: query GitHub Actions / GitLab CI for last 3 workflow runs on
{monitored_repos} using gh CLI or API.
Eval: any run in "failure" or "cancelled" state in last 2h?
If yes: send Telegram "🚨 CI failed: {repo}/{workflow} — {error_summary}" with link.
State: track last-seen run IDs.
```

**[HB-10] Uptime check**
```
Spawn subagent: HTTP GET {monitored_urls} list with 10s timeout.
Check: status code 200-299, response time < {latency_threshold_ms}.
Eval: any URL non-200 OR latency > threshold?
If yes: send Telegram "🔴 Down: {url} — {status_code} ({latency}ms)"
Run: every 5 min during business hours, every 30 min overnight.
```

**[HB-11] Open PRs**
```
Spawn subagent: list open PRs on {repos} via gh CLI. Filter to PRs:
- authored by {team_members} AND open > 2 days with no review
- OR marked "needs review" AND no activity in 24h
Eval: any stale PR matching criteria?
If yes: send Telegram "🔁 Stale PR: {title} ({days}d open) — {link}"
Run: every 4h during business hours.
```

**[HB-12] Error rate spike**
```
Spawn subagent: query {monitoring_source} (Datadog/Sentry/CloudWatch) for error
rate on {service_name} over last 15 min. Compare to 7-day p75 baseline.
Eval: current error rate > baseline * {spike_multiplier} (default 3x)?
If yes: send Telegram "🚨 Error spike: {service} {rate}/min vs baseline {baseline}/min"
State: store last baseline value.
```

